  "title": "Erdős Problem #529",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "Let $d_k(n)$ be the expected distance from the origin after taking $n$ random steps from the origin in $\\mathbb{Z}^k$ (conditional on no self intersections) - that is, a self-avoiding walk. Is it true that $ \\lim_{n\\to \\infty}\\frac{d_2(n)}{n^{1/2}}= \\infty? $ Is it true that $ d_k(n)\\ll n^{1/2} $ for $k\\geq 3$?",
